# Why does the comparison work?

/* Commentary layer only. C = attributed commentator claim; R = supplied editorial bridge or comparison. All arrows are editorial. The base Gemara maps remain separate. See sources/commentary.json. */

/* C | Rashi | Rashi on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. ואיסורא דומיא דהיתירא | Base nodes: R2, R3 */
[KR1 · Rashi: the same verse]: C · Ordinary return and exceptional acquisition come from one verse, warranting their comparison. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KR6 · Supplied: make the extra premise visible>

/* C | Rashi | Rashi on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. אף איסורא | Base nodes: R4, R6 */
[KR2 · Rashi: the timing limit]: C · Ordinary unmarked loss is prohibited here when the owner may not have learned of the loss before the finder took it. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KR6 · Supplied: make the extra premise visible>

/* C | Tosafot | Tosafot on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. איסורא דומיא דהתירא | Base nodes: R1, R2 */
[KR3 · Tosafot: why a special verse?]: C · Known despair already permits ordinary loss. A river verse confined to that case would add nothing. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> [KR4 · Tosafot: what the exception adds]

/* C | Tosafot | Tosafot on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. איסורא דומיא דהתירא | Base nodes: R1, R2 */
[KR4 · Tosafot: what the exception adds]: C · The river permission therefore reaches lack of awareness, even with a mark and even where learning would not produce despair. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> [KR5 · Tosafot: carry across the comparison]

/* C | Tosafot | Tosafot on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. איסורא דומיא דהתירא | Base nodes: R3, R4, R6 */
[KR5 · Tosafot: carry across the comparison]: C · The ordinary prohibition likewise covers absence of known despair, with or without a mark; prior despair before pickup remains the route to permission. {"color": "#53659c"}
  +> <KR6 · Supplied: make the extra premise visible>

/* R | Editorial | Rashi on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. ואיסורא דומיא דהיתירא; Rashi on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. אף איסורא; Tosafot on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. איסורא דומיא דהתירא | Base nodes: R3, R4, R5, R6 */
<KR6 · Supplied: make the extra premise visible>: R · Join the same-verse comparison to Tosafot’s redundancy reasoning and preserve Rashi’s timing limit. River permission alone is insufficient. {"color": "#f3d5a5"}

/* C | Tosafot | Tosafot on Bava Metzia 22b, s.v. תיובתא דרבא | Base nodes: R7 */
[KR7 · Tosafot: Rava knew the baraita]: C · Rava knew the river source but had not drawn the prohibition–permission comparison. This explains the refutation, rather than adding a proof. {"color": "#53659c"}

